ural alabama the  only lawyer that the two can rely on is  one of the new yorker's cousins who only  recently passed the bar and has no  experience working on a trial marissa  tomei plays the fiance of the lawyer  helping the friends mona lisa vito her  performance is a standout in the film  even winning her the academy award for  best supporting actress several decades  later tomei would play aunt may in the  mcu's spider-man series alongside tom  holland making her first appearance in  captain america civil war tomae is the  third person to play on may in live  action following up rosemary harris in  the toby maguire trilogy and sally field  in the andrew garfield duology it's so  hard for me to believe that she's  someone's aunt yeah well we come in all  shapes and sizes you know the mcu  features many versions of classic  characters that differ from their  original appearances the ancient one a  powerful sorcerer who serves as a mentor  to dr strange was depicted as a male in  many of the comics 2016's doctor strange  introduced a different version of the  character an androgynous guru portrayed  by tilda swinton swinton has only been  nominated for the academy award once but  once was all that she needed to win best  supporting actress for her performance  in the 2007 legal drama michael clayton  it is unclear if the ancient one will  ever return as the character didn't make  an appearance in doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness  australian actress kate blanchett has  been nominated for the academy award  seven times the first time she won an  oscar was for best supporting actress  for her portrayal of catherine hepburn  in martin scorsese's the aviator her  second oscar and first for best actress  came from her performance as former  socialite jasmine francis in the woody  allen comedy blue jasmine in the marvel  cinematic universe blanchett played  thor's sister hella who is released from  prison after the death of odin during  the events of thor ragnarok she serves  as the main villain of the movie  destroying thor's hammer killing the  warriors three and taking over asgard  before she's finally dispatched believe  me i would love for someone else to rule  but it can't be you you're just  the worst  taika waititi directed thor ragnarok and  voices the hilarious alien court  injecting some of his signature humor  into the fantasy film series why tt  returns to the franchise in thor love  and thunder both as director and chord  after ytt directed the mcu film he wrote  directed and starred in the historical  comedy film jojo rabbit he played an  imaginary version of adolf hitler who  tries to influence a ten-year-old boy  after he discovers a jewish girl hiding  in his house from the nazis the film was  nominated for several oscars and waititi  won the academy award for best adapted  screenplay  2018's black panther represented several  firsts for the mcu it was the first film  in the series with the predominantly  black cast and the first mcu film to be  nominated for best picture it was also  the first superhero movie overall to  receive a nomination in that category  the film features several black actors  who have both won academy awards prior  to the film and after one of those  actors was lupita nyong'o who played  black panther's partner in spy nakia  nyong'o was fortunate enough to win the  academy award for best supporting  actress in the first theatrical film she  started she won for her portrayal of  patsy in the historical drama 12 years a  slave which also won best picture  nyong'o hasn't been nominated since but  has also been busy starring as maz  kanata in the star wars sequel trilogy  and voicing raksha in the remake of the  jungle book  forest whitaker made his film debut in  1982 with both tagged the assassination  game and fast times at richmond high  since then whitaker has been in a number  of acclaimed movies one of these was the  film the last king of scotland which  centered around a doctor played by james  mcavoy who was assigned to take care of  the real-life ugandan president edie  umeen whitaker's performance as  president amin received praise from  critics and he ended up winning the  academy award for best actor when  whitaker made his mcu debut in black  panther he played the elderly states  minzuri who guided king t'challa  spiritually with the help of a special  heart-shaped herb unfortunately because  the character of zuri died during the  events of the film whitaker will not  return for black panther wakanda forever  unlike lupita nyong'o and forest  whitaker british actor daniel kaluya won  an oscar after he made his mcu debut his  performance as black panther party  chairman fred hampton the subject of the  film judas and the black messiah won him  the academy award for best supporting  actor it was the second time kaluyo was  nominated for an academy award he was  previously nominated for best actor for  his performance as chris washington in  jordan pales debut horror film get out  i can't move  you can't move  in black panther kaluya plays wakabi the  man charged with defending the borders  of the fictional kingdom of wakanda  despite initially pledging loyalty to  t'challa and being married to dora  malachi head okoye wakabi betrays both  of them and joins forces with killmonger  2019's captain marvel was the last mcu  film before the avengers team reunited  in avengers in-game bree lawson  portrayed the titular superhero also  known as carol danvers a pilot infused  with special powers who uses them to  save the alien skrulls from her former  employer the film established captain  marvel as one of the most powerful  characters in the mcu and someone who  would play a key role in future marvel  films larson has been a cast member in  several acclaimed movies but her best  work comes in the film room the picture  tells the story of ma a woman who  escapes seven years of captivity with  her young son and must adjust her life  back in 