ural alabama the  only lawyer that the two can rely on is  one of the new yorker's cousins who only  recently passed the bar and has no  experience working on a trial marissa  tomei plays the fiance of the lawyer  helping the friends mona lisa vito her  performance is a standout in the film  even winning her the academy award for  best supporting actress several decades  later tomei would play aunt may in the  mcu's spider-man series alongside tom  holland making her first appearance in  captain america civil war tomae is the  third person to play on may in live  action following up rosemary harris in  the toby maguire trilogy and sally field  in the andrew garfield duology it's so  hard for me to believe that she's  someone's aunt yeah well we come in all  shapes and sizes you know the mcu  features many versions of classic  characters that differ from their  original appearances the ancient one a  powerful sorcerer who serves as a mentor  to dr strange was depicted as a male in  many of the comics 2016's doctor strange  introduced a different version of the  character an androgynous guru portrayed  by tilda swinton swinton has only been  nominated for the academy award once but  once was all that she needed to win best  supporting actress for her performance  in the 2007 legal drama michael clayton  it is unclear if the ancient one will  ever return as the character didn't make  an appearance in doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness  australian actress kate blanchett has  been nominated for the academy award  seven times the first time she won an  oscar was for best supporting actress  for her portrayal of catherine hepburn  in martin scorsese's the aviator her  second oscar and first for best actress  came from her performance as former  socialite jasmine francis in the woody  allen comedy blue jasmine in the marvel  cinematic universe blanchett played  thor's sister hella who is released from  prison after the death of odin during  the events of thor ragnarok she serves  as the main villain of the movie  destroying thor's hammer killing the  warriors three and taking over asgard  before she's finally dispatched believe  me i would love for someone else to rule  but it can't be you you're just  the worst  taika waititi directed thor ragnarok and  voices the hilarious alien court  injecting some of his signature humor  into the fantasy film series why tt  returns to the franchise in thor love  and thunder both as director and chord  after ytt directed the mcu film he wrote  directed and starred in the historical  comedy film jojo rabbit he played an  imaginary version of adolf hitler who  tries to influence a ten-year-old boy  after he discovers a jewish girl hiding  in his house from the nazis the film was  nominated for several oscars and waititi  won the academy award for best adapted  screenplay  2018's black panther represented several  firsts for the mcu it was the first film  in the series with the predominantly  black cast and the first mcu film to be  nominated for best picture it was also  the first superhero movie overall to  receive a nomination in that category  the film features several black actors  who have both won academy awards prior  to the film and after one of those  actors was lupita nyong'o who played  black panther's partner in spy nakia  nyong'o was fortunate enough to win the  academy award for best supporting  actress in the first theatrical film she  started she won for her portrayal of  patsy in the historical drama 12 years a  slave which also won best picture  nyong'o hasn't been nominated since but  has also been busy starring as maz  kanata in the star wars sequel trilogy  and voicing raksha in the remake of the  jungle book  forest whitaker made his film debut in  1982 with both tagged the assassination  game and fast times at richmond high  since then whitaker has been in a number  of acclaimed movies one of these was the  film the last king of scotland which  centered around a doctor played by james  mcavoy who was assigned to take care of  the real-life ugandan president edie  umeen whitaker's performance as  president amin received praise from  critics and he ended up winning the  academy award for best actor when  whitaker made his mcu debut in black  panther he played the elderly states  minzuri who guided king t'challa  spiritually with the help of a special  heart-shaped herb unfortunately because  the character of zuri died during the  events of the film whitaker will not  return for black panther wakanda forever  unlike lupita nyong'o and forest  whitaker british actor daniel kaluya won  an oscar after he made his mcu debut his  performance as black panther party  chairman fred hampton the subject of the  film judas and the black messiah won him  the academy award for best supporting  actor it was the second time kaluyo was  nominated for an academy award he was  previously nominated for best actor for  his performance as chris washington in  jordan pales debut horror film get out  i can't move  you can't move  in black panther kaluya plays wakabi the  man charged with defending the borders  of the fictional kingdom of wakanda  despite initially pledging loyalty to  t'challa and being married to dora  malachi head okoye wakabi betrays both  of them and joins forces with killmonger  2019's captain marvel was the last mcu  film before the avengers team reunited  in avengers in-game bree lawson  portrayed the titular superhero also  known as carol danvers a pilot infused  with special powers who uses them to  save the alien skrulls from her former  employer the film established captain  marvel as one of the most powerful  characters in the mcu and someone who  would play a key role in future marvel  films larson has been a cast member in  several acclaimed movies but her best  work comes in the film room the picture  tells the story of ma a woman who  escapes seven years of captivity with  her young son and must adjust her life  back in the real world larson's  performance was lauded by critics and it  won her the academy award for best  actress among several other nominations  and wins  casting for a comic book adaptation  doesn't get any more perfect than j.k  simmons as daily bugle publisher jay  jonah jameson simmons ability to deliver  hilarious lines we still remember today  made him one of the best aspects of sam  raimi's spider-man trilogy in the 2000s  you don't trust anybody that's your  problem i trust my barber  in 2019 spider-man far from home simmons  reprised his role as jameson to once  again terrorize spider-man in a  completely different franchise but  simmons is much more than just jay jonah  jameson he has also been nominated for  and won several awards simmons was  recently nominated for best supporting  actor for his portrayal of william  frawley in aaron sorkins being the  ricardo's about lucille ball's  relationship with desi arnette during  the height of i love lucy he won the  oscar previously for playing the abusive  music teacher terence fletcher in damien  chazelle's whiplash  after she played a supporting role in  several different mcu films 2021's black  widow finally gave natasha romanoff the  solo movie that she deserved not only  did we get to learn more about the  character's past but we also got to meet  the other members of the family that she  had before she was trained as an  assassin and later joined the avengers  natasha's adoptive mother molina vasikov  is played by english actress rachel  weiss weiss has been nominated for the  academy award for best supporting  actress twice her first nomination which  resulted in a win was for playing tessa  abbott quail in the constant gardener  her character's murder is what main  protagonist justin quail played by rath  finds is trying to solve her second  nomination was for the favorite playing  queen anne's advisor and manipulative  love sarah churchill who battles emma  stone's abigail mashem for the queen's  approval and affection  there we go  marvel movies don't get more epic than  oscar winner chloe zhao's 2021 superhero  film eternals the film follows a group  of extraterrestrials across thousands of  years as they work to defend earth from  other alien invaders one of the core  members of the group is thina a warrior  eternal who can create weapons out of  cosmic energy dina is played by angelina  jolie who has been nominated for the  academy award twice and was even honored  with the gene herschel humanitarian  award for her work outside of film jolie  earned her academy award for her work as  psychiatric patient lisa rowe in the  drama girl interrupted winning for best  supporting actress the second time jolie  was nominated was for best actress in  changelit in this drama by clint  eastwood she plays a mother whose son  gets kidnapped only to have a different  child return to her  there are two post-credit scenes in  eternals that introduce several new  characters the first is the introduction  of harry styles arrows known as star fox  in the comics the second gives us a hint  of kit harington's black knight but  before fans are able to see more of the  character a voice from off-screen  interrupts him before the screen cuts to  black  sure you're ready for that mr whitman  that voice is our first tease of  mahershala ali's portrayal of blade a  vampire hunter previously portrayed by  western snipes in the original blade  trilogy ali has already been in the mcu  before playing the villain cottonmouth  in the luke cage series outside of his  marvel projects ali has been nominated  for and won best supporting actor twice  the first was for playing drug dealer  wan in moonlight and the second was for  playing don shirley in green book his  first win made ali the first muslim to  ever win an acting oscar  the mcu has expanded across all of time  and space so it seems only natural that  the franchise would start crossing into  different universes as well we got  glimpses of this in the disney plus show  loki but 2021 spider-man no way home  took it to the next level when peter  parker had to face off against super  villains from the past two spider-man  film series first introduced in the  amazing spider-man 2 max dillon was an  underappreciated oz corp employee before  an accident transformed him into the  super villain electro jamie foxx played  the character in his original debut  before returning to the role in no way  home fox has been nominated twice for  academy awards both in the same year his  best supporting actor nom was for  playing max the cab driver in collateral  and his best actor nom was for playing  ray charles in the biopic ray fox won  the best actor award but lost supporting  actor to morgan freeman for his  performance in million dollar baby on  march 13 2022 acclaimed actor william  hurt died at the age of 71 due to  complications from prostate cancer hurt  was nominated for the academy award four  times the first three of which were  consecutive and all being for best actor  in a leading role these films were kiss  of the spider woman which he won  children of a lesser god and broadcast  news his fourth and final nomination  came for a supporting role in david  croninberg's a history of violence in  the marvel cinematic universe hurt  played thaddeus ross originally debuting  in the incredible hulk back when edward  norton played bruce banner instead of  mark ruffalo ross was promoted from us  general to secretary of state he was one  of the driving forces behind the sokovia  accords that divided the avengers in  captain america civil war you can also  find him in avengers infinity war  avengers in game and black widow  remembered as one of the best films of  2011 the descendants is a dramedy about  an attorney who needs to make some  serious changes in his life after his  wife ends up in a coma after a boating  accident the film went on to get five  nominations at the academy awards  winning for best adapted screenplay this  would mark the second win for co-writer  and director alexander payne and the  first win for the other two co-writers  matt faxon and jim rash rash has  co-written and co-directed two other  films after the descendants alongside  faxen and also received praise for his  role as dean craig pelton in nbc's  community rash also made a brief  appearance in captain america civil war  as a staff member of mit it makes sense  considering that directors joe and  anthony russo directed several episodes  of community before jumping into the mcu  the mcu television shows on disney plus  have taken fans to many different places  one division turned the marvel universe  into a classic sitcom while loki  introduced several different versions of  the fan favorite character moon knight  offers an even wilder tale following the  multiple personalities of the titular  hero whether it's the mercenary mark  spector or museum employee steven grant  both are heavily influenced by the  egyptian god khanshu kareem al-hakim  provided the onset performance for  khanshu while f murray abraham voiced  the character you might know abraham  from homeland or the grand budapest  hotel but his most revered work happened  several years prior the 1984 film  amadeus told the story of wolf gang  amadeus mozart and his rivalry with  composer antonio salieri the latter  character was played by abraham who won  the academy award for best actor for his  performance the film would eventually go  on to win an additional seven academy  awards including best picture  doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness is filled with cameos and  special appearances alternate versions  of past superheroes and the mcu debut of  patrick stewart's professor charles  xavier from the x-men series one of the  film's post-credit scenes had one more  surprise up its sleeve though when all  was said and done doctor strange was  approached by the sorceress clia for a  special mission involving an incursion  that must be stopped clear was played by  charlize theron who has been nominated  for the academy award for best actress  three times she won her first nomination  for playing serial killer eileen warnos  in 2003's monster her next two  nominations came from her roles in north  country and bombshell both films telling  stories of women fighting against sexual  harassment in the workplace you've  called women you don't like  fat pigs  dogs  slobs and disgusting animals  between her work as cipher in the fast  and furious series and her potentially  big role as clia theron will definitely  be busy for a while  you can always count on english actor  christian bale to turn in a stellar  acting performance especially  considering the controversial physical  transformations he goes through for some  of these roles from the weight he gained  for his role as irving rosenfeld in  american hustle and dick cheney in vice  to the weight he lost for the machinist  in rescue don he's never been afraid to  embrace a full-body makeover the  transformations worked as he was  nominated for the academy award for best  actor for the first two bale was also  nominated for best supporting actor for  playing michael bury in the big short  and dickie eklund in the fighter winning  for the latter bale is one of the many  actors to portray batman doing so in  christopher nolan's dark knight trilogy  a decade after the final film in the  trilogy was released bale has returned  to the world of superheroes as gore the  god butcher in taiko ytt's thor love and  thunder  bale and portman aren't the only big  names joining the mcu with thor love and  thunder perhaps the biggest new face is  russell crowe who will be playing the  olympian king zeus like bale crowe had  experience in dc films before making the  jump to the mcu playing superman's  father jorel and man of steel from 2000  to 2002 crow was nominated for best  actor three times he earned praise for  his roles in the insider and a beautiful  mind and he won for his role as maximus  decimus meridius in riley scott's  gladiator  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

